### (c) Lambda-a0 at face value
 G1 (i) paper alpha 0.8, a0 = a_Lambda/0.8: kappa_eff 0.5758, +0.0613 dex [FAIL G1]; a0 1.0784e-10
 G1 (ii) alpha 1, a0 = a_Lambda: kappa_eff 0.4607, -0.0356 dex [PASS G1]; a0 8.6269e-11
 G1 (iii) model as written, a0 = fitted W3 constant (a): kappa_eff 0.3363 (-0.1722 dex) -- a fit, not a tie; alpha = a_Lambda/a0 = 1.370
 alpha implied by lib A0: a_Lambda/A0 = 0.921 (paper quotes ~0.8, provisional)
 G2 slope: as written W0 = Lambda/8 pi G and W3 = 32 pi^2 G^2/a0 are independent constants -> 0 [FAIL G2]; naturalness imposed -> 0.5 [PASS G2 by hand, 1 hand term]
 G3 a(z)/a(0) (Lambda and W3 constant, a0 does not follow H): 1.0: 1.00, 1.5: 1.00, 2.33: 1.00 [PASS G3]
 G4 one constant across hosts: universal W coefficient [PASS G4 by construction]; G5 operative at galaxy radii via W3 [PASS G5]
 (c) verdict: NO NATIVE TIE -- relation is an order-of-magnitude naturalness claim, not derived; G2 only by hand; G1 passes only at alpha = 1, not at the paper's 0.8

Not run: relativistic cosmology of the dipolar medium, CMB, clusters, Solar System with external field, ghost analysis.
Rival language. Passing shows freedom, not evidence. kappa = 1/2 FITTED; not theory closed.
